# Commit-identity advisory. MUST NEVER BLOCK — and both halves of that are
# structural here rather than a promise in a comment (Rowan RC 3416):
#
#   * it runs BEFORE lint-staged, so the hook's exit status stays
#     lint-staged's. Appended after it, this line became the hook's status and
#     silently turned lint-staged into a no-op — a failing lint exited 0 and
#     the commit went through. That is a worse defect than the one the
#     advisory exists to warn about.
#   * it is guarded on presence AND executability, and its status is
#     discarded. Called bare, a missing file exits 127 and a non-executable
#     one exits 126, either of which BLOCKS the commit — the exact opposite of
#     what this is for, and reachable by a bad checkout rather than by malice.
#
# See .githooks/check-commit-identity.sh and docs/agents/commit-identity.md.
# The gate is review, not this.
if [ -x ./.githooks/check-commit-identity.sh ]; then
  ./.githooks/check-commit-identity.sh || true
fi

# Last, and its status is the hook's: lint-staged IS a gate.
pnpm lint-staged
